# `tools/build_standalone.mjs --check` is step 11 of the gate and compares the generated
# standalone brief against a fresh rebuild with plain string equality. The builder emits the
# lines it generates itself with bare LF while inheriting CRLF from the source, and git's
# autocrlf then rewrites every line to CRLF on checkout -- so on Windows the check passes
# immediately after a build and fails after any checkout, though `git diff` shows the content
# identical. Pinning both files to LF makes the comparison hold on every platform.
docs/brief.standalone.html    eol=lf
system/web/brief/index.html   eol=lf

# Every tracked generated file is LF, on both sides of the round trip.
#
# Two halves, and the first version of this rule had only one of them. The check-out half:
# `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the working tree, so a generator emitting LF leaves
# `git status` reporting files modified while `git diff` shows no content change -- a tree that
# is dirty after every green gate is a tree in which nobody reads `git status`, and a real
# uncommitted change goes unnoticed among the false ones. `eol=lf` fixes that side.
#
# The write half: the generators must actually emit LF. `tools/harvest.mjs` does. The Python
# cutters did NOT -- `Path.write_text` defaults to `newline=None`, which translates "
" to
# `os.linesep`, and that is CRLF here. Measured: running `make_placeholders.py` unpinned put 743
# carriage returns into the placeholder slice and dirtied two tracked files, with `eol=lf`
# already in force. `eol=lf` normalises on check-in, so the blob stays LF, but it does not stop
# the working tree going modified. Both halves are needed, and the second lives in the scripts:
# every `write_text` under `system/backend/scripts/` passes `newline=""`. A new generator that
# writes a tracked path needs the same, and its path listed below. See D89 and D91.
data/content/*.json           eol=lf
data/slices/**/*.json         eol=lf
data/golden/*.json            eol=lf
data/predictions/**/*.json    eol=lf
data/vlm/**/*.json            eol=lf
data/mini-isg/*.json          eol=lf
